/span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">det_monoid_automaton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lq</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">δ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rcases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The idea is to obtain a witness y proving x is in Set.range lq in order to return lq (u*y).<br>\nHowever, the usual approaches of obtain, rcases and let expressions have not worked for me so far.<br>\nThe errors I am getting are along the lines of \"Tactic <code>cases</code> failed with a nested error:<br>\nTactic <code>induction</code> failed: recursor <code>Exists.casesOn</code> can only eliminate into <code>Prop</code>\"<br>\nI am not sure what to make of this.<br>\nHelp would be appreciated.</p>",
